<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of the Netherlands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Netherlands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of the Netherlands is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> monarchy established in 1815 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>, succeeding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. It governed the later phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">decolonisation</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. The name Netherlands is also used on the site for the Dutch lands more generally, including their trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Netherlands" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
